# The milestone's code-health cleanup, step A (run.sh's f72m): Properties' count of a folder holding a
# mount point (d/m, a stand-in sshfs in the mount list, a file in it): the mount point is counted as a
# folder and never looked at, as a dead share's root would hang the walk (fstatat came before the
# drive check). d/e, an ordinary folder beside it, is counted all the way down.
settle
wait-for 2000 n=1 sel=d
key ctrl-i
wait-for 3000 propdone=1 propdirs=3 propfiles=1 propbytes=3 propcut=0 propname=d
quit
